WEBVTT

1
00:00:13.134 --> 00:00:18.545
"The boys from the next town are playing Paper Chase today," said Bobbie one morning.

2
00:00:18.546 --> 00:00:21.050
"Perks thinks they'll run along the railway line.

3
00:00:21.051 --> 00:00:22.888
We can go and watch."

4
00:00:22.889 --> 00:00:27.571
Mother gave the children some lunch, and they left.

5
00:00:27.572 --> 00:00:32.939
There were men working on the tracks, using different tools like spades and shovels.

6
00:00:32.940 --> 00:00:35.866
The children watched them for awhile.

7
00:00:35.867 --> 00:00:39.599
Then a voice said, "Let me pass, please."

8
00:00:39.600 --> 00:00:42.400
It was the first boy from the school.

9
00:00:42.401 --> 00:00:47.163
"He's 'it.'" Bobbie explained the game to her brother and sister.

10
00:00:47.164 --> 00:00:50.074
"All the other boys have to chase after him."

11
00:00:50.075 --> 00:00:54.742
Under the boy's arm was a bag full of little pieces of paper.

12
00:00:54.743 --> 00:00:59.070
The boy dropped a piece of paper behind him for the other boys to follow.

13
00:00:59.071 --> 00:01:04.960
The children watched as he ran into the long dark tunnel, dropping more paper behind him.

14
00:01:04.961 --> 00:01:07.281
The workmen watched him too.

15
00:01:07.282 --> 00:01:10.399
"He shouldn't go in there," said one.

16
00:01:10.400 --> 00:01:13.812
"It's only a game," said another.

17
00:01:13.813 --> 00:01:19.161
Then the other boys came, running and following the little white pieces of paper.

18
00:01:19.162 --> 00:01:23.327
Bobbie and Phyllis and Peter counted the boys as they ran past.

19
00:01:23.328 --> 00:01:25.672
There were thirty of them.

20
00:01:25.673 --> 00:01:29.849
The boys ran into the tunnel and disappeared into the deep darkness.

21
00:01:29.850 --> 00:01:32.642
The last boy wore a red shirt.

22
00:01:32.643 --> 00:01:36.676
"It's not easy running in the dark," said one of the workmen.

23
00:01:36.677 --> 00:01:41.057
"How long will it take?" Peter asked, eyeing the long tunnel.

24
00:01:41.058 --> 00:01:43.190
It went through a hill.

25
00:01:43.191 --> 00:01:48.095
"An hour or more," the man said.

26
00:01:48.096 --> 00:01:51.722
"Let's go across the top of the hill," said Peter.

27
00:01:51.723 --> 00:01:54.939
"We can watch the boys come out the other end."

28
00:01:54.940 --> 00:01:59.535
The children climbed up the steep hill, over rocks and tree trunks.

29
00:01:59.536 --> 00:02:04.421
"It's like climbing the Alps!" said Bobbie, out of breath.

30
00:02:04.422 --> 00:02:06.983
At last they reached the top.

31
00:02:06.984 --> 00:02:12.131
Peter lay down on the grass, and the girls lay down too.

32
00:02:12.132 --> 00:02:14.901
After a while Bobbie sat up.

33
00:02:14.902 --> 00:02:17.037
"Look!" she cried.

34
00:02:17.038 --> 00:02:19.537
"What?" said Phyllis.

35
00:02:19.538 --> 00:02:24.074
"The view," said Bobbie.

36
00:02:24.075 --> 00:02:26.823
"Let's go now," said Peter.

37
00:02:26.824 --> 00:02:31.132
"But this view is fantastic!" insisted Bobbie.

38
00:02:31.133 --> 00:02:36.959
They could see the fields, the village, the station and even their white house.

39
00:02:36.960 --> 00:02:40.893
"We'll miss the paper chase!" said Phyllis impatiently.

40
00:02:40.894 --> 00:02:43.267
"Come on. Let's go."

41
00:02:43.268 --> 00:02:48.325
They climbed down until they were level with the top of the tunnel. They waited.

42
00:02:48.326 --> 00:02:54.672
"The boys have all gone past already, of course," said Phyllis, annoyed.

43
00:02:54.673 --> 00:02:58.054
"I don't think so," said Bobbie.

44
00:02:58.055 --> 00:03:02.449
"But even if they have, there's a wonderful view here too!

45
00:03:02.450 --> 00:03:05.563
We can see the trains come out of the tunnel.

46
00:03:05.564 --> 00:03:11.085
We've never seen the trains from on top before."

47
00:03:11.086 --> 00:03:15.554
"Look, here he comes!" Peter shouted at last.

48
00:03:15.555 --> 00:03:19.731
The first boy with the paper came slowly out of the tunnel.

49
00:03:19.732 --> 00:03:22.338
Soon after came the other boys.

50
00:03:22.339 --> 00:03:24.703
Some looked very tired.

51
00:03:24.704 --> 00:03:28.136
"What will we do now?" asked Bobbie.

52
00:03:28.137 --> 00:03:31.223
"That's not the last one," Peter said.

53
00:03:31.224 --> 00:03:34.153
"Where's the boy in the red shirt?"

54
00:03:34.154 --> 00:03:37.772
They waited a long time, but the boy did not appear.

55
00:03:37.773 --> 00:03:42.466
The children began to worry, and they climbed down to the train tracks.

56
00:03:42.467 --> 00:03:47.092
"Perhaps he had an accident," said Phyllis.

57
00:03:47.093 --> 00:03:50.226
"Let's go and look," said Bobbie.

58
00:03:50.227 --> 00:03:53.770
They slowly walked a few steps into the dark tunnel.

59
00:03:53.771 --> 00:03:56.722
But they couldn't see a boy in a red shirt.

60
00:03:56.723 --> 00:04:00.642
It was very dark and water dripped down the wall.

61
00:04:00.643 --> 00:04:11.426
"I don't like it in here!" said Phyllis, looking frightened.
